---
// Homepage - v2 "editorial depth" skin on the approved wireframe structure.
// Copy is canon (PRD rule 6). Styles: src/styles/home.css, tokens only.
// v1 design export archived at design-briefs/styled-homepage-v1.html.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import OptInForm from '../components/OptInForm.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';

// $97 session sells via the standalone landing page (decided 2026-07-12).
// Off-domain for now; swap to the on-domain "/session" port here when it ships.
const SESSION_URL = 'https://abq-landing-v2.vercel.app';
---

<Base
  title="Quit Smoking or Vaping With Always Be Quitting"
  description="Coaching and community from a certified tobacco treatment specialist with 25 years of experience."
>
  {/* 0 · announcement + nav */}
  <SiteHeader />

  {/* 1 · hero - HEADLINE + ONE LINE, NOTHING ELSE (Jon, 2026-08-14).
       Matches the live site exactly: no sub-headline, no trust line, no opt-in.
       Design phase: full-bleed environmental photograph, both lines on a scrim.
       "You've tried before" needs statement weight, not kicker size. */}
  <header class="band band--paper hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="display-xl hl">
        Make This Your Last Attempt to Quit Smoking or Vaping, <em>Not Just Your Next One</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="kicker kicker--under">You've tried before. It didn't last.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  {/* 1b · Quick-Start Guide opt-in - its own section directly below the hero,
       per the live site. Moved out of the hero 2026-08-14. Band treatment TBD
       in the design phase (live site uses a sage field here). */}
  {/* 🚨 id="sub_ABQtips" IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT RENAME OR REMOVE IT.

       Every description on Jon's YouTube channel (~50 videos) links to
       https://www.alwaysbequitting.com/#sub_ABQtips, carried over from the
       systeme.io site. Those descriptions are the channel's only route to the
       list, and editing 50 of them is not a realistic fix.

       A fragment is never sent to the server, so this CANNOT be handled by a
       redirect the way the old page URLs were. The anchor has to physically
       exist in the homepage markup or the link silently lands at the top of
       the page instead of the form. Verified present in the build. */}
  <section id="sub_ABQtips" class="band band--white optin-band" style="scroll-margin-top: 90px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <OptInForm returnTo="/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 2 · recognition */}
  <section class="band band--paper recognition">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="lead reveal">
        <h2 class="display-lg hl">You try to quit. It doesn't last. Months later you try again - <em>and the cycle repeats.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You can't seem to start.</h3>
          <p>You know you want to quit. You've thought about it for months, maybe years. But the moment to actually do it never quite arrives.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You're struggling to stay quit.</h3>
          <p>You made it a few days, weeks, or longer. But the cravings, the stress, the routines keep pulling you back, and you can feel yourself slipping.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You've already quit and want it to last.</h3>
          <p>You stopped smoking or vaping, but you're worried about going back. You want to make sure it sticks this time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
          <h3>You've relapsed and want to try again.</h3>
          <p>It already happened. You're frustrated, tired of the cycle, and ready for something different. You want to try again, but smarter this time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 3 · transformation */}
  <section class="band band--teal transform">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <h2 class="display-xl" style="margin-top: var(--gap-sm)">
        Temporary abstinence isn't quitting - <span class="sweep"><em>transformation is.</em></span>
      </h2>
      {/* Last sentence replaced 2026-08-23 (Jon). Was "That's why nothing here
          promises you'll quit in X days" - meta-commentary about the site's own
          editorial policy rather than anything about the reader, and defensive
          at a point where the objection has not been raised, which plants it.
          "Improve your odds" is deliberate: it promises effort, not outcome,
          which keeps this inside PRD site rule 3. Do not harden it into a
          results claim. */}
      <p>
        Stopping can happen fast. Staying quit is a months-long transformation.
        That's why everything here is built to improve your odds of staying quit for life.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 4 · what makes the difference */}
  <section class="band band--white recognition" style="margin-top:0">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding-block: var(--section) 0">
      <h2 class="display-lg hl" style="margin-top: var(--gap-sm)">Here's What Makes <em>The Difference</em></h2>
      <div class="grid grid--4" style="margin-block: 2.4rem 5rem">
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Expert Guidance</h3>
          <p>from someone who knows the many paths to quitting</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Real Accountability</h3>
          <p>when cravings hit and you want to give in</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Ongoing Motivation</h3>
          <p>to keep you moving forward</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card card--pop reveal">
          <h3>Mindset Transformation</h3>
          <p>that helps you stay quit for life</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 5a · GUIDE - EMPATHY. StoryBrand splits the Guide into two distinct beats:
       empathy ("I understand what this feels like") then authority ("and I am
       competent to get you out of it"). Miller keeps them separate because a
       guide who only empathises is a friend, and one who only shows credentials
       is a salesman.

       SPLIT RESTORED 2026-08-23 (Jon), matching the live site. The build had
       melted both beats into one section and demoted the authority heading -
       "Get help from someone who has been successfully guiding people through
       quitting for decades" - to a 0.95rem grey caption under the empathy
       paragraph, so the second beat never announced itself and the three stats
       appeared with nothing framing them.
       DO NOT recombine these two sections. */}
  <section class="band band--paper guide">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="guide__row reveal">
        {/* HIERARCHY SWAPPED 2026-08-23 (Jon) - "option B".

            The empathy/authority sentence is Jon's canonical StoryBrand Guide
            soundbite, recorded verbatim in voice.md beat 3: "I understand how
            discouraging this struggle is. I've helped all types of people quit
            successfully, and I can help you, too." It was set as grey --soft
            body copy underneath a heading that is really just a label, so the
            one sentence the framework says must land was the smallest thing in
            the section.

            "I'm Jon, and I provide exactly that kind of support" is NOT deleted
            and must not be - "exactly that kind of support" is a deliberate
            callback to the four items in "What Makes The Difference" directly
            above (homepage-spec item 5). It becomes the kicker so the bridge
            survives while the substance takes the display type. */}
        <div>
          {/* class renamed guide__kicker -> guide__intro 2026-08-26. It is an
              introduction, not an eyebrow label, and the old name is what led
              to it being styled as one. */}
          <p class="guide__intro">I'm Jon, and I provide exactly that kind of support.</p>
          <h2 class="display-lg guide__statement">
            I know how discouraging your struggle is. I've spent 25 years helping people who thought they could
            never quit smoking or vaping - quit for life. And <em>I can help you, too.</em>
          </h2>
        </div>
        {/* Jon's headshot, added 2026-08-23. Source was a 1.2MB PNG at
            1080x1350; encoded to WebP at 560px (17KB) with a 2x for retina and
            a JPG fallback. Despite the source filename it has NO alpha channel -
            the background is baked-in white, which is fine here because the
            photo sits in a white card on a tinted band, as on the live site.
            Aspect is 4/5 (0.8) and .guide__photo matches it, so nothing crops. */}
        <picture class="guide__photo">
          <source
            type="image/webp"
            srcset="/img/jon-headshot.webp 1x, /img/jon-headshot@2x.webp 2x"
          />
          <img
            src="/img/jon-headshot.jpg"
            width="560"
            height="700"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Jon Fritsch, CTTS and NCNTT certified tobacco treatment specialist"
          />
        </picture>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 5b · GUIDE - AUTHORITY. Still its own section (see 5a), but the heading is
       gone - removed 2026-08-23 (Jon).

       It read "Get help from someone who has been successfully guiding people
       through quitting for decades" and made the same claim as the empathy
       paragraph above it ("I've spent 25 years...") and the first stat card
       ("25 Years - ...CTTS and NCNTT certified specialist"). Three statements of
       one claim inside about twenty words of reading; PRD rule 5b calls
       redundancy within a page a defect. The numbers announce themselves.

       DELIBERATE divergence from the live site, which does carry the heading.
       Do not restore it on the grounds that live has it. */}
  {/* Band colour RESOLVED 2026-08-26. This was band--paper as a placeholder, to
      stop the stats running into the white offers section below. It is now
      band--white as part of the site-wide white/mist alternation, and the
      separation still holds because the section after it is mist. */}
  <section class="band band--white authority">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat reveal"><b>25 Years</b><span>helping people quit smoking and vaping as a CTTS and NCNTT certified specialist</span></div>
        <div class="stat reveal"><b>3 Decades</b><span>teaching informative, effective, and engaging health workshops</span></div>
        <div class="stat reveal"><b>35 Years</b><span>creating programs that help people change their behavior</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 6a · WHAT JON OFFERS - the two levels of service, named plainly, no prices.
       Added 2026-08-14 (Jon). The old single "Start for $97" section was doing two
       jobs at once - announcing the offerings AND the entry price - so neither
       service registered and the page read as one product with two buttons.
       Offer-architecture rule 1: visitors self-select their level of service. */}
  <section class="band band--paper offers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-lg hl">Two ways to <em>work with me.</em></h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="offer reveal">
          <h3>The ABQ Community</h3>
          <p>Weekly live Q&amp;A calls with Jon and 24/7 access to a community of people quitting alongside you. Move forward at your own pace, with support and accountability the whole way. You don't even have to be ready to quit to start.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/community">See how the community works</a>
        </div>
        <div class="offer reveal">
          <h3>1:1 Coaching</h3>
          {/* Names that ongoing 1:1 work exists WITHOUT naming or pricing the
               $1,200 Program - keeps the 2026-07-12 PRD decision intact.
               Assembled from Jon's language: "Jon in your corner" (offer-architecture),
               "no one-size-fits-all programs" (trust line), relapse-as-path (FAQ voice). */}
          <p>Working with me directly, one to one, over the months a real transformation takes. Not a one-size-fits-all program - a plan built around your life, with me in your corner between sessions, for the slips as much as the wins.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/coaching">See how 1:1 coaching works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 6b · WHAT $97 BUYS. Price lives here only; 6a does the describing.

       REFRAMED 2026-08-23 (Jon) from a RATE claim, not an ENTRY claim. The old
       heading was "Either way, you start for $97" - written when the community
       was genuinely $97/month billed monthly. It is now $291 up front, so that
       sentence had become FALSE for one of the two doors: someone read $97,
       clicked Join, and was asked for $291.

       The current heading works because "starts at $97 a month" describes a
       RATE and a price level - not a first payment. $97 IS the community's
       monthly rate (billed 3 up front) and IS the session price, so it is true
       on both sides. Each card states the actual charge directly beneath, so the
       rate and the amount are never separated.

       🚨 DO NOT reintroduce "your first month", "start for $97", or "what it
       costs to begin". All three are entry-price claims, and there is no $97
       transaction for the community - the smallest purchase is $291. Two
       rewrites have already drifted back into this; it reads naturally and is
       false. Only rate wording survives.

       Card copy is intentionally thin - price, terms, button. Describing the
       services here is 6a's job, and the previous version had drifted into
       repeating 6a almost verbatim ("24/7 access to people quitting alongside
       you", "You don't have to be ready to quit to start"). Keep it out. */}
  <section class="band band--white band--dots doors">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="doors__mega reveal" aria-hidden="true">$97</div>
      {/* "a month" not "per month" (Jon, 2026-08-23): parallels "a session" in
          the second half, and "per month" is invoice register - voice.md asks
          for human, not clinical. The precise form ($97/month) lives on the card
          below, which is where it belongs. */}
      <h2 class="display-lg hl">Working with me starts at $97 a month in the community, or <em>$97 for a session, just the two of us.</em></h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        <div class="door door--community reveal">
          <h3>The ABQ Community</h3>
          {/* ALWAYS keep "paid up front" next to the rate (Jon, 2026-08-21) -
               without it this reads as a monthly subscription and the price
               appears to triple when they reach /community. */}
          <div class="price">$97/month</div>
          <p class="door__terms">3 months, $291 paid up front.</p>
          <ul class="door__list">
            <li>Weekly live calls with Jon, all recorded</li>
            <li>24/7 access to people quitting alongside you</li>
            <li>Quit at your own pace - no rigid timeline</li>
            <li>You don't have to be ready to quit to start</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn--cta" href="/community">Join the Community</a>
        </div>
        <div class="door door--session reveal">
          {/* This line exists to stop the card competing with 6a's 1:1 card
              (Jon, 2026-08-23). 6a describes ongoing 1:1 work - the $1,200
              Program, deliberately unnamed - while this sells a single session.
              Two different products under near-identical names read as one
              service described twice, so this card has to be openly the small
              door. Keep it a taster; do not let it grow into a Program pitch. */}
          <h3>A 1:1 Session with Jon</h3>
          <div class="price">$97 one-time</div>
          <p class="door__terms">One per person.</p>
          <ul class="door__list">
            {/* "written plan" removed 2026-08-23 (Jon): it implies a document
                and a complete quit strategy out of 50 minutes, which the session
                cannot reliably deliver. Replaced with the thing that actually
                differentiates a conversation from an app or a pamphlet - advice
                tailored to the person. Uses Jon's existing "one-size-fits-all"
                language. Do NOT reintroduce "plan" here. */}
            <li>A private 50-minute conversation</li>
            <li>Ask me anything - what's kept you stuck, what to try next</li>
            <li>Advice tailored to you, not a one-size-fits-all program</li>
            <li>The simplest way to work with me directly</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn--cta" href={SESSION_URL}>Book your $97 session</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="doors__mitigate reveal">$97 is less than most people spend in a single month (or week) on smoking or vaping.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 7 · proof - TESTIMONIALS ARE VERBATIM FROM THE LIVE SITE, RESTORED IN FULL
       2026-08-23 (Jon). A previous pass had cut them to one or two sentences
       each - Katherine went from 110 words to 22 - with no recorded decision.

       The cuts kept the vaguest line and deleted the two that sell:
         "It took me nearly six years to build the courage to find a specialist"
           - the reader's own situation, the empathy hook
         "If you have reservations about investing in a coach, I cannot
           recommend Jon enough" - the buying objection answered by a customer
           rather than by Jon

       Length is deliberate (Jon): a tidy one-liner reads as marketing-written,
       while a long rambling paragraph with a face and a name reads as a real
       person - and that signal lands whether or not anyone reads the words.
       DO NOT TRIM THESE. If they are too long for the layout, the layout
       changes; see design-punchlist.md. */}
  <section class="band band--paper proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: var(--gap-md)">
        {/* Testimonial photos added 2026-08-23 (Jon), matching the live site,
            which shows a headshot with every testimonial.

            The CSS circle (.quote__photo, border-radius 50%) is doing real work
            beyond looks - the three source images are inconsistent:
              - Kait      : a plain 806x870 photo, cropped square here
              - Ashley    : pre-circled PNG with GENUINE transparency
              - Katherine : pre-circled with SOLID WHITE corners, no alpha
            Clipping to a circle in CSS hides Katherine's white corners, so all
            three present identically on any band colour.

            ⚠️ Katherine remains constrained: her corners are gone from the
            source, so if the design phase wants square or rounded-rect photos
            she needs a fresh export from the original. Logged in
            design-punchlist.md. */}
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>It took me nearly six years to build the courage to find a specialist and I am unbelievably grateful it was Jon. I felt like I was constantly at war with myself, and Jon became my outlet, a safe person who helped me negotiate that struggle. He provided reassuring research, perspectives, and options I could take. What surprised me most was his approach - he acted as my biggest supporter, providing perfect guidance when quitting became extremely challenging. If you have reservations about investing in a coach, I cannot recommend Jon enough. The impact he has had on my life is transformative.</blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            <picture>
              <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/katherine-headshot.webp" />
              <img class="quote__photo" src="/img/katherine-headshot.jpg" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Katherine R." />
            </picture>
            <span><b>Katherine R.</b> · One Year Vape Free</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>Jon's non-assuming approach and meeting me where I was at was really helpful. He helped break the all-or-nothing thinking for me. Our conversations often ended in "well just try it out and see what happens." He came in with curiosity, and just getting to understand where I was at, so that he could help me. Having the support and the accountability - it's kind of two sides of the same coin. That was probably one of the pieces that I was missing. And that wasn't something I was necessarily going to seek out on my own.</blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            <picture>
              <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/kait-headshot.webp" />
              <img class="quote__photo" src="/img/kait-headshot.jpg" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Kait" />
            </picture>
            <span><b>Kait</b> · 9 Years Sober, Now Smoke-Free</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>I've invited Jon to teach about tobacco treatment to my university class for 9 straight semesters. He provides valuable insights into tobacco addiction &amp; cessation and also offers practical and realistic strategies on how to assist clients. His presentations are informative, entertaining and inspiring. I've had students tell me they actually quit using tobacco after attending them.</blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            <picture>
              <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/ashley-headshot.webp" />
              <img class="quote__photo" src="/img/ashley-headshot.jpg" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Ashley Foster, MPH, RD, CHES" />
            </picture>
            <span><b>Ashley Foster, MPH, RD, CHES</b> · University Professor</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* FAQ section removed entirely (Jon, 2026-08-14). Objection-handling belongs
       on /community and /coaching, where the decision is actually made; the
       homepage had enough text. Nothing from it was relocated. */}


  {/* 8b · STAKES - StoryBrand beat 7 (Failure), placed immediately before the
       final ask so the stakes land while the CTA is in view. Copy is Jon's,
       verbatim, approved 2026-08-14.
       NOTE: the "physically and mentally sick" sentence is a deliberate,
       Jon-approved exception to the voice.md DON'T "fear-of-death or
       medical-scare messaging." Recorded in voice.md - do not "fix" it. */}
  <section class="band band--white stakes">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <p class="display-lg stakes__body">
        You can continue to spend $1k, $2k, $3k, $4k every year on cigarettes and vapes.
        You can continue to make yourself physically and mentally sick.
        And next year at this time, you'll wish you had started today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 9 · final cta */}
  <section class="band band--navy final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-xl hl">Always be quitting, <em>until you've quit for the last time.</em></h2>
      <div class="final__actions reveal">
        <a class="btn btn--cta" href="/community">Join the Community</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={SESSION_URL}>Book a $97 Session</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 10 · footer */}
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
